+
+**Exact target (claim type `bounded_theorem`).**
+- T1 (two-level domination): from the all-`a` plane the coarse-grained dissent `ξ_x = 1{v_x ≠ a}` is dominated by the two-level noisy majority automaton `η'`: `η'_x = 1` if at least two predecessors are `1`; otherwise `η'_x = 1{U_x < ε₂}` if exactly one predecessor is `1` and `1{U_x < ε₁}` if none, with `ε₁ = d_1`, `ε₂ = max(d_2, d_3)` and i.i.d. uniforms `U`.
+- T2 (the extended explanation tree): every `1` of `η'` at `x` has a subtree of `G` through `1`-sites with at most one arrow to a predecessor per node, whose nodes without such an arrow (the seeds `S`) have no `1`-predecessor, whose amplified nodes `A` have exactly one (their arrow's end), and whose other nodes have two; with `forks = |S| − 1` and excuse arrows `E ≤ 3(|S| − 1) + 2|A|`. (Block 25's construction with the amplified nodes inside the clusters; an amplified pole's excuse is its single predecessor; the charge equal to that predecessor's direction loses one unit of span — a bad pair — and bad amplified poles are kept; the potential accounting.)
+- T3 (the count and the bound): `P(η'_x = 1) ≤ ε₁·R(t + ε₂/t², ε₁/t³)` for every `t ∈ (0, 1]` with the point in the recursion's domain (`R` block 25's recursion; the amplified arrows share the arrow slots; the budget turns `ε₂^{|A|}` into `(ε₂/t²)^{|A|}`).
+- T4 (the region): exact rational super-solutions at `p = 4165` on `(p, 1, 2)`, `2085` on `(p, 1, 1)`, `8330` on `(p, 2, 4)`, `6247` on `(p, 1, 3)`; six invariant laws there (block 25's T7 route restated).
+- T5 (the ceiling): the recursion's domain at `y → 0` is `x < 4/27` (tangency of `U = (1 + xU)³`), so the route needs `ε₂ < max_t t²(4/27 − t) = 256/531441 ≈ 4.8·10⁻⁴`; on `(p, 1, 2)` this is `p > 4150` whatever `ε₁`: the route is at its ceiling; the remaining gap to the located `11` is a factor `380`, attributed to the bad-pair accounting (`2` excuse arrows per amplified pole; the executed trees use at most `2/3`) and to the count's overcounting of sub-structures.
+- Executed: the extended construction on every configuration of the depth-2 cone, all depth-3 configurations with `≤ 4` noise sites and random cones (tree, classification, budgets, the potential accounting); the certificates exactly; the brackets `p₀ − 1` fail.
+
+**Falsifiers.** A configuration where the extended construction fails or a budget is exceeded; a certificate inequality failing; `ε(p₀ − 1)` admitted; a domain point beyond `4/27` at `y = 0`.
+
+**Lens pass.** *"Why not the count?"* It is at its edge (block 25 sharpened); the domination is the loose step by `10⁴` at the located strength. *"Is the amplified node a noise node?"* It is a `1` with one `1`-predecessor, so its uniform is below `ε₂` — paid `ε₂`; treating it as a leaf would charge its fork at `ε₂/t³` and lose everything; putting it inside the cluster costs the bad pairs. *"The tree-of-trees alternative (fresh trees under amplified leaves, weight `ε₂` with no bad pairs) would reach `p ≈ 200`."* Its sub-trees overlap the structure and the overlaps break the budgets; recorded under N1 as the next obstacle. *"Names."* Only in the allowed sections.
